{
  "title": "12: Yusuf يوسف",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nالٓرٰ تِلْكَ اٰيٰتُ الْكِتٰبِ الْمُبِيْن‏(1)\nALAARAA TILKA AAYAATUL KETAABE AL-MUBEEN.\nA.L.R. These are the symbols (or Verses) of the perspicuous Book. \nاِنَّاۤ اَنْزَلْنٰهُ قُرْءٰنًا عَرَبِيًّا لَّعَلَّكُمْ تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(2)\nINNAA ANZALNAAHO QURAANAN A’RABIYYAL LA-A’LLAKUM TA’QELOON.\nWe have sent it down as an Arabic Qur'an, in order that ye may learn wisdom. \nنَحْنُ نَقُصُّ عَلَيْكَ اَحْسَنَ الْقَصَصِ بِمَاۤ اَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ هٰذَا الْقُرْاٰنَ ۖ وَاِنْ كُنْتَ مِنْ قَبْلِهٖ لَمِنَ الْغٰفِلِيْنَ‏(3)\nNAHNO NAQUSSU A’LAYKA AHSANAL AL-QASASE BEMAA AAWHAYNAA ELAYKA HAAZAL QURAANA WA KUNTA MIN QABLEHI LAMENAS AL-GHAAFELEENA.\nWe do relate unto thee the most beautiful of stories, in that We reveal to thee this (portion of the) Qur'an: before this, thou too was among those who knew it not. \nاِذْ قَالَ يُوْسُفُ لِاَبِيْهِ يٰۤاَبَتِ اِنِّىْ رَاَيْتُ اَحَدَ عَشَرَ كَوْكَبًا وَّالشَّمْسَ وَالْقَمَرَ رَاَيْتُهُمْ لِىْ سٰجِدِيْنَ‏(4)\nIZ QAALA YOOSUFU LEAABEEHE YAA INNEE RAAYTU AAHADA A’ASHARA KAWKABAN WWAALSSHAMSA WAL QAMARA RAAYTUHUM LEE SAAJEDEENA.\nBehold! Joseph said to his father: “O my father! I did see eleven stars and the sun and the moon: I saw them prostrate themselves to me!” \nقَالَ يٰبُنَىَّ لَا تَقْصُصْ رُءْيَاكَ عَلٰٓى اِخْوَتِكَ فَيَكِيْدُوْا لَكَ كَيْدًا ؕ اِنَّ الشَّيْطٰنَ لِلْاِنْسَانِ عَدُوٌّ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(5)\nQAALA YAABUNAA LAA TAQSUS RUYAAKA A’LAA AEKHWATEKA FAYAKEEDOOA LAKA KAYDAANW INNAL ASH-SHAYTAANA INSAANIK A’DUWWUM MOBEEN.\nSaid (the father): “My (dear) little son! relate not thy vision to thy brothers, lest they concoct a plot against thee: for Satan is to man an avowed enemy! \nوَكَذٰلِكَ يَجْتَبِيْكَ رَبُّكَ وَيُعَلِّمُكَ مِنْ تَاْوِيْلِ الْاَحَادِيْثِ وَيُتِمُّ نِعْمَتَهٗ عَلَيْكَ وَعَلٰٓى اٰلِ يَعْقُوْبَ كَمَاۤ اَتَمَّهَا عَلٰٓى اَبَوَيْكَ مِنْ قَبْلُ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ وَاِسْحٰقَ ؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ عَلِيْمٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(6)\nWA KAZAALEKA YAJTABEEKA RABBOKA WAYUA’ALLEMUKA MIN TAAWEELE AL-AAHAADEESE WAYUTEMMU NE’MATAHU A’LAYKA WA A’LAA AALE YA’QOOBAL KAMAA AATAMMAHAA A’LAA AABAWAYKA MIN QABLO IBRAAHEEMA WA ISHAAQA INNAL RABBAKA A’LEEM HAKEEM.\n“Thus will thy Lord choose thee and teach thee the interpretation of stories (and events) and perfect His favour to thee and to the posterity of Jacob - even as He perfected it to thy fathers Abraham and Isaac aforetime! for Allah is full of knowledge and wisdom.” \nلَقَدْ كَانَ فِىْ يُوْسُفَ وَاِخْوَتِهٖۤ اٰيٰتٌ لِّلسَّآئِلِيْنَ‏(7)\nLAQAD KAANA FEE YOOSUFA WAAKHWATEH AAYAATUM LLELSSAAELEENA.\nVerily in Joseph and his brethren are signs (or symbols) for seekers (after Truth). \nاِذْ قَالُوْا لَيُوْسُفُ وَاَخُوْهُ اَحَبُّ اِلٰٓى اَبِيْنَا مِنَّا وَنَحْنُ عُصْبَةٌ  ؕ اِنَّ اَبَانَا لَفِىْ ضَلٰلٍ مُّبِيْنِ ۖ ۚ‏(8)\nIZ QAALOO LAYOOSUFU WAAKHOOHU AAHABBU ELAA AABEENAA MINNAA WA NAHNO U’USBATUN INNA AABAANAA LAFEE ZALAALIM MMUBEENE.\nThey said: “Truly Joseph and his brother are loved more by our father than we: But we are a goodly body! really our father is obviously wandering (in his mind)! \nاۨقْتُلُوْا يُوْسُفَ اَوِ اطْرَحُوْهُ اَرْضًا يَّخْلُ لَكُمْ وَجْهُ اَبِيْكُمْ وَ تَكُوْنُوْا مِنْۢ بَعْدِهٖ قَوْمًا صٰلِحِيْنَ‏(9)\nAQTULOOA YOOSUFA AWE’ ATRAHOOHU AARZAN YYAKHLU LAKUM WAJHUL AABEEKUM WA TAKOONOO MIN BA’DEHI QAWMAN SAALEHEENA.\n“Slay ye Joseph or cast him out to some (unknown) land, that so the favour of your father may be given to you alone: (there will be time enough) for you to be righteous after that!” \nقَالَ قَآئِلٌ مِّنْهُمْ لَا تَقْتُلُوْا يُوْسُفَ وَاَلْقُوْهُ فِىْ غَيٰبَتِ الْجُبِّ يَلْتَقِطْهُ بَعْضُ السَّيَّارَةِ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ فٰعِلِيْنَ‏(10)\nQAALA QAAELUN MINHUM LAA TAQTULOOA YOOSUFA WAALQOOHU FEE GHAYBATE AL-JUBBE YALTAQETHU BA’ZUL AS-SAYARATE IN KUNTUM FAAE’ELEENA.\nSaid one of them: “Slay not Joseph, but if ye must do something, throw him down to the bottom of the well: he will be picked up by some caravan of travellers.” \nقَالُوْا يٰۤاَبَانَا مَا لَكَ لَا تَاْمَنَّا عَلٰى يُوْسُفَ وَاِنَّا لَهٗ لَنٰصِحُوْنَ‏(11)\nQAALOO YAABAANAA MAA LAKA LAA TAAMANNAA A’LAA YOOSUFA WA INNAA LAHU LANAASEHOONA.\nThey said: “O our father! why dost thou not trust us with Joseph, seeing we are indeed his sincere well-wishers? \nاَرْسِلْهُ مَعَنَا غَدًا يَّرْتَعْ وَيَلْعَبْ وَاِنَّا لَهٗ لَحٰفِظُوْنَ‏(12)\nAARSELHU MAA’ANAA GHADAN YYARTAA’ WAYALA’AB WA INNAA LAHU LAHAAFEZOONA.\n“Send him with us tomorrow to enjoy himself and play, and we shall take every care of him.” \nقَالَ اِنِّىْ لَيَحْزُنُنِىْ اَنْ تَذْهَبُوْا بِهٖ وَاَخَافُ اَنْ يَّاْكُلَهُ الذِّئْبُ وَاَنْتُمْ عَنْهُ غٰفِلُوْنَ‏(13)\nQAALA INNEE LAYAHZUNUNEAA AN TAZHABOOA BEHI WA AKHAAFO AN YYAAKULAHU AZ-ZEBU WA ANTUM A’NHO GHAAFELOON.\n(Jacob) said: “Really it saddens me that ye should take him away: I fear lest the wolf should devour him while ye attend not to him.” \nقَالُوْا لَئِنْ اَكَلَهُ الذِّئْبُ وَنَحْنُ عُصْبَةٌ اِنَّاۤ اِذًا لَّخٰسِرُوْنَ‏(14)\nQAALOO LAIL AAKALAHU AZ-ZEBU WA NAHNO U’USBATUN INNAA EZAL LLAKHAASEROONA.\nThey said: “If the wolf were to devour him while we are (so large) a party, then should we indeed (first) have perished ourselves!” \nفَلَمَّا ذَهَبُوْا بِهٖ وَاَجْمَعُوْۤا اَنْ يَّجْعَلُوْهُ فِىْ غَيٰبَتِ الْجُبِّۚ وَاَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلَيْهِ لَتُنَبِّئَنَّهُمْ بِاَمْرِهِمْ هٰذَا وَهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُوْنَ‏(15)\nFALAMMAA ZAHABOOA BEHI WAAJMAU’OOA AN YYAJA’ALOOHU FEE GHAYBATE AL-JUBBE WA AWHAYNAA ELAYHE LATUNABBEANNAHUM BE-AMREHIM HAAZAA WA HUM LAA YASH-O’ROON.\nSo they did take him away, and they all agreed to throw him down to the bottom of the well: and We put into his heart (this Message): 'Of a surety thou shalt (one day) tell them the truth of this their affair while they know (thee) not' \nوَجَآءُوْۤ اَبَاهُمْ عِشَآءً يَّبْكُوْنَؕ‏(16)\nWA JAAA-OO AABAAHUM E’ESHAAAN YYABKOONA.\nThen they came to their father in the early part of the night, weeping. \nقَالُوْا يٰۤاَبَانَاۤ اِنَّا ذَهَبْنَا نَسْتَبِقُ وَتَرَكْنَا يُوْسُفَ عِنْدَ مَتَاعِنَا فَاَكَلَهُ الذِّئْبُۚ وَمَاۤ اَنْتَ بِمُؤْمِنٍ لَّنَا وَلَوْ كُنَّا صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(17)\nQAALOO YAABAANAA INNAA ZAHABNAA NASTABEQU WATARAKNAA YOOSUFA I’NDAL MATAAE’ENAA FAAKALAHU AZ-ZEBU WA MAA ANTA BEMUMENIN LANAA WA LAW KUNNAA SAADEQEEN.\nThey said: “O our father! We went racing with one another, and left Joseph with our things; and the wolf devoured him.... But thou wilt never believe us even though we tell the truth.” \nوَجَآءُوْ عَلٰى قَمِيْصِهٖ بِدَمٍ كَذِبٍؕ قَالَ بَلْ سَوَّلَتْ لَكُمْ اَنْفُسُكُمْ اَمْرًاؕ فَصَبْرٌ جَمِيْلٌؕ وَاللّٰهُ الْمُسْتَعَانُ عَلٰى مَا تَصِفُوْنَ‏(18)\nWA JAAA-OO A’LAA QAMEESEH BEDAMIN KAZEBIN QAALA BAL SAWLAT LAKUM ANFOSOKUM AAMRAN FASABRUN JAMEELUN WAL LAAHO AL-MUSTAA’AANU A’LAA MAA TASEFOONA.\nThey stained his shirt with false blood. He said: “Nay, but your minds have made up a tale (that may pass) with you, (for me) patience is most fitting: Against that which ye assert, it is Allah (alone) Whose help can be sought”.. \nوَجَآءَتْ سَيَّارَةٌ فَاَرْسَلُوْا وَارِدَهُمْ فَاَدْلٰى دَلْوَهٗ ؕ قَالَ يٰبُشْرٰى هٰذَا غُلٰمٌ ؕ وَاَسَرُّوْهُ بِضَاعَةً  ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌۢ بِمَا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(19)\nWA JAAA-AT SAYARATUN FAARSALOOA WAAREDAHUM FAADLAA DALWAH QAALA YAABUSHRAA HAAZAA GHULAAMUN WAASARROOHU BEZAAA’ATAN WAL LAAHO A’LEEM BEMAA YA’MALOON.\nThen there came a caravan of travellers: they sent their water-carrier (for water), and he let down his bucket (into the well)...He said: “Ah there! Good news! Here is a (fine) young man!” So they concealed him as a treasure! But Allah knoweth well all that they do! \nوَشَرَوْهُ بِثَمَنٍۢ بَخْسٍ دَرَاهِمَ مَعْدُوْدَةٍ ۚ وَكَانُوْا فِيْهِ مِنَ الزّٰهِدِيْنَ‏(20)\nWASHARAWHU BESAMANIN BAKHSIN DARAAHEMA MAA’DOODATIN WA KAANOO FEEHE MENAL AZ-ZAAHEDEENA.\nThe (Brethren) sold him for a miserable price, for a few dirhams counted out: in such low estimation did they hold him! \nوَقَالَ الَّذِى اشْتَرٰٮهُ مِنْ مِّصْرَ لِامْرَاَتِهٖۤ اَكْرِمِىْ مَثْوٰٮهُ عَسٰٓى اَنْ يَّنْفَعَنَاۤ اَوْ نَتَّخِذَهٗ وَلَدًا ؕ وَكَذٰلِكَ مَكَّنَّا لِيُوْسُفَ فِى الْاَرْضِوَلِنُعَلِّمَهٗ مِنْ تَاْوِيْلِ الْاَحَادِيْثِؕ وَاللّٰهُ غَالِبٌ عَلٰٓى اَمْرِهٖ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(21)\nWA QAALA LAZIS TARAAHO MIM MMESRA LEAMRAATEH AAKREMEAA MASWAAHU A’SAA AN YYANFAA’ANAA AW NATTAKHEZAH LAAHO WA KAZAALEKA MAKKANNAA LEEWSUFA FIL AL-AARZEWALENUA’ALLEMAH MIN TAAWEELE AL-AAHAADEESE WAL LAAHO GHAALEBUN A’LAA AMREHI LAAKINNAL AKSARAN NAASE LAA YA’LAMOON.\nThe man in Egypt who bought him, said to his wife: “Make his stay (among us) honourable: may be he will bring us much good, or we shall adopt him as a son.” Thus did We establish Joseph in the land, that We might teach him the interpretation of stories (and events). And Allah hath full power and control over His affairs; but most among mankind know it not. \nوَلَمَّا بَلَغَ اَشُدَّهٗۤ اٰتَيْنٰهُ حُكْمًا وَّعِلْمًا ؕ وَكَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(22)\nWA LAMMAA BALAGHA ASHUDDAHU AATAYNAAHO HUKMAWN WA I’LMAA WA KAZAALEKA NAJZIL MOHSENEEN.\nWhen Joseph attained His full manhood, We gave him power and knowledge: thus do We reward those who do right. \nوَرَاوَدَتْهُ الَّتِىْ هُوَ فِىْ بَيْتِهَا عَنْ نَّفْسِهٖ وَغَلَّقَتِ الْاَبْوَابَ وَقَالَتْ هَيْتَ لَكَؕ قَالَ مَعَاذَ اللّٰهِ اِنَّهٗ رَبِّىْۤ اَحْسَنَ مَثْوَاىَؕ اِنَّهٗ لَا يُفْلِحُ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ‏(23)\nWARAAWADATHU LATEE HOWA FEE BAYTEHAA A’N NNAFSEH WAGHALLAQATE AL-AABWAABA WA QAALAT HAYTA LAK QAALA MAA’AAZA LAAHE INNAHU RABBEE AHSANAL MASWAAAAA INNAHU LAA YUFLEHUZ ZAALEMOON.\nBut she in whose house he was, sought to seduce him from his (true) self: she fastened the doors, and said: “Now come, thou (dear one)!” He said: “Allah forbid! truly (thy husband) is my lord! he made my sojourn agreeable! truly to no good come those who do wrong!” \nوَلَقَدْ هَمَّتْ بِهٖۚ وَهَمَّ بِهَا لَوْلَاۤ اَنْ رَّاٰ بُرْهَانَ رَبِّهٖؕ كَذٰلِكَ لِنَصْرِفَ عَنْهُ السُّۤوْءَ وَالْفَحْشَآءَؕ اِنَّهٗ مِنْ عِبَادِنَا الْمُخْلَصِيْنَ‏(24)\nWA LAQAD HAMMAT BEHI WAHAMMA BEHAA LAWLAA AR RRAA BURHAANA RABBEH KAZAALEKA LENASREFA A’NHO AS-SOOA WAL FAHSHAAA INNAHU MIN E’EBAADENAA AL-MUKHLASEENA.\nAnd (with passion) did she desire him, and he would have desired her, but that he saw the evidence of his Lord: thus (did We order) that We might turn away from him (all) evil and shameful deeds: for he was one of Our servants, sincere and purified. \nوَاسْتَبَقَا الْبَابَ وَقَدَّتْ قَمِيْصَهٗ مِنْ دُبُرٍ وَّاَلْفَيَا سَيِّدَهَا لَدَا الْبَابِؕ قَالَتْ مَا جَزَآءُ مَنْ اَرَادَ بِاَهْلِكَ سُوْۤءًا اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يُّسْجَنَ اَوْ عَذَابٌ اَلِيْمٌ‏(25)\nWAASTABAQAA BAABA WAQADDAT QAMEESAH MIN DUBURIN WWAALFAYAA SAYDAHAA LADAA AL-BAABE QAALAT MAA JAZAAA-O MAN ARAADA BEAAHLEKA SOOAN ILLAA AN YYUSJANA AW A’ZAABUN ALEEM.\nSo they both raced each other to the door, and she tore his shirt from the back: they both found her lord near the door. She said: “What is the (fitting) punishment for one who formed an evil design against thy wife, but prison or a grievous chastisement?” \nقَالَ هِىَ رَاوَدَتْنِىْ عَنْ نَّفْسِىْ وَشَهِدَ شَاهِدٌ مِّنْ اَهْلِهَاۚ اِنْ كَانَ قَمِيْصُهٗ قُدَّ مِنْ قُبُلٍ فَصَدَقَتْ وَهُوَ مِنَ الْكٰذِبِيْنَ‏(26)\nQAALA HEYA RAAWADATNEAA A’N NNAFSEAA WA SHAHEDA SHAAHEDUN MIN AHLEHAA IN KAANA QAMEESUH QUDDA MIN QUBULIN FASADAQAT WA HOWA MENAL KAAZEBEEN.\nHe said: “It was she that sought to seduce me - from my (true) self.” And one of her household saw (this) and bore witness, (thus):- “If it be that his shirt is rent from the front, then is her tale true, and he is a liar! \nوَاِنْ كَانَ قَمِيْصُهٗ قُدَّ مِنْ دُبُرٍ فَكَذَبَتْ وَهُوَ مِنَ الصّٰدِقِيْنَ‏(27)\nWA KAANA QAMEESUH QUDDA MIN DUBURIN FAKAZABAT WA HOWA MENAL SAADEQEENA.\n“But if it be that his shirt is torn from the back, then is she the liar, and he is telling the truth!” \nفَلَمَّا رَاٰ قَمِيْصَهٗ قُدَّ مِنْ دُبُرٍ قَالَ اِنَّهٗ مِنْ كَيْدِكُنَّؕ اِنَّ كَيْدَكُنَّ عَظِيْمٌ‏(28)\nFALAMMAA RAA QAMEESAH QUDDA MIN DUBURIN QAALA INNAHU MIN KAYDEKUNNA INNA KAYDAKUNNA A’ZEEM.\nSo when he saw his shirt, that it was torn at the back, (her husband) said: “Behold! It is a snare of you women! truly, mighty is your snare! \nيُوْسُفُ اَعْرِضْ عَنْ هٰذَا وَاسْتَغْفِرِىْ لِذَنْۢبِكِ ۖ ۚ اِنَّكِ كُنْتِ مِنَ الْخٰطِٮئِيْنَ‏(29)\nYOOSUFU AAA’REZ A’N HAAZAA WAASTAGHFEREAA LEZANBEKE AENNAKE KUNTE MENAL AL-KHAATEEENA.\n“O Joseph, pass this over! (O wife), ask forgiveness for thy sin, for truly thou hast been at fault!” \nوَقَالَ نِسْوَةٌ فِى الْمَدِيْنَةِ امْرَاَتُ الْعَزِيْزِ تُرَاوِدُ فَتٰٮهَا عَنْ نَّفْسِهٖۚ قَدْ شَغَفَهَا حُبًّا ؕ اِنَّا لَنَرٰٮهَا فِىْ ضَلٰلٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(30)\nWA QAALA NESWATUN FIL MADEENATE AMRAATU A’ZEEZIL TURAAWEDU FATAAHAA A’N NNAFSEH QAD SHAGHAFAHAA HUBBAL INNAA LANARAAHAA FEE ZALAALIM MOBEEN.\nLadies said in the City: “The wife of the (great) 'Aziz is seeking to seduce her slave from his (true) self: Truly hath he inspired her with violent love: we see she is evidently going astray.” \nفَلَمَّا سَمِعَتْ بِمَكْرِهِنَّ اَرْسَلَتْ اِلَيْهِنَّ وَاَعْتَدَتْ لَهُنَّ مُتَّكَاً وَّاٰتَتْ كُلَّ وَاحِدَةٍ مِّنْهُنَّ سِكِّيْنًا وَّقَالَتِ اخْرُجْ عَلَيْهِنَّ ۚ فَلَمَّا رَاَيْنَهٗۤ اَكْبَرْنَهٗ وَقَطَّعْنَ اَيْدِيَهُنَّ وَقُلْنَ حَاشَ لِلّٰهِ مَا هٰذَا بَشَرًا ؕ اِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا مَلَكٌ كَرِيْمٌ‏(31)\nFALAMMAA SAMEA’AT BEMAKREHENNA AARSALAT AELAYHENNA WAAA’TADAT LAHUNNA MUTTAKAA WWAATAT KULLA WAAHEDATIN MIN-HUNNA SEKKEENAN WA QAALATIN AKHRUJ A’LAYHINNA FALAMMAA RAAYNAH AAKBARNAH WAQATTAA’NA AAYDEEHUNNA WAQULNA HAASHA LILLAAHE MAA HAAZAA BASHARAN IN HAAZAA ILLAA MALAKUN KAREEM.\nWhen she heard of their malicious talk, she sent for them and prepared a banquet for them: she gave each of them a knife: and she said (to Joseph), “Come out before them.” When they saw him, they did extol him, and (in their amazement) cut their hands: they said, “Allah preserve us! no mortal is this! this is none other than a noble angel!” \nقَالَتْ فَذٰلِكُنَّ الَّذِىْ لُمْتُنَّنِىْ فِيْهِؕ وَ لَقَدْ رَاوَدْتُّهٗ عَنْ نَّفْسِهٖ فَاسْتَعْصَمَؕ وَلَئِنْ لَّمْ يَفْعَلْ مَاۤ اٰمُرُهٗ لَيُسْجَنَنَّ وَلَيَكُوْنًا مِّنَ الصّٰغِرِيْنَ‏(32)\nQAALAT FAZAALEKUNNA LAZEE LUMTUNNANEAA FEEH WA LAQAD RAAWADTTUH A’N NNAFSEH FAASTAA’SAMA WA LAIN LAM YAFA’AL MAA AAAMURUH LAYUSJANANNA WALAYAKOONAN MENAL AS-SAAGHEREENA.\nShe said: “There before you is the man about whom ye did blame me! I did seek to seduce him from his (true) self but he did firmly save himself guiltless!....and now, if he doth not my bidding, he shall certainly be cast into prison, and (what is more) be of the company of the vilest!” \nقَالَ رَبِّ السِّجْنُ اَحَبُّ اِلَىَّ مِمَّا يَدْعُوْنَنِىْۤ اِلَيْهِۚ وَاِلَّا تَصْرِفْ عَنِّىْ كَيْدَهُنَّ اَصْبُ اِلَيْهِنَّ وَاَكُنْ مِّنَ الْجٰهِلِيْنَ‏(33)\nQAALA RABBIL AS-SEJNU AAHABBU ELAYYA MIMMAA YADU’OONANEAA ELAYHE WA ILLAA TASREF A’NNEE KAYDAHUNNA AASBU AELAYHENNA WA AKUM MENAL JAAHELEEN.\nHe said: “O my Lord! the prison is more to my liking than that to which they invite me: Unless Thou turn away their snare from me, I should (in my youthful folly) feel inclined towards them and join the ranks of the ignorant.” \nفَاسْتَجَابَ لَهٗ رَبُّهٗ فَصَرَفَ عَنْهُ كَيْدَهُنَّؕ اِنَّهٗ هُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْعَلِيْمُ‏(34)\nFAASTAJAABA LAHU RABBOHU FASARAFA A’NHO KAYDAHUNNA INNAHU HOWA SAMEE-U’L A’LEEM.\nSo his Lord hearkened to him (in his prayer), and turned away from him their snare: Verily He heareth and knoweth (all things). \nثُمَّ بَدَا لَهُمْ مِّنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا رَاَوُا الْاٰيٰتِ لَيَسْجُنُنَّهٗ حَتّٰى حِيْنٍ‏(35)\nSUMMA BADAA LAHUM MIM BA’DE MAA RAAWUA AAYAATE LAYASJUNUNNAH HATTAA HEEN.\nThen it occurred to the men, after they had seen the signs, (that it was best) to imprison him for a time. \nوَدَخَلَ مَعَهُ السِّجْنَ فَتَيٰنِؕ قَالَ اَحَدُهُمَاۤ اِنِّىْۤ اَرٰٮنِىْۤ اَعْصِرُ خَمْرًا ۚ وَقَالَ الْاٰخَرُ اِنِّىْۤ اَرٰٮنِىْۤ اَحْمِلُ فَوْقَ رَاْسِىْ خُبْزًا تَاْكُلُ الطَّيْرُ مِنْهُ ؕ نَبِّئْنَا بِتَاْوِيْلِهٖ ۚ اِنَّا نَرٰٮكَ مِنَ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(36)\nWA DAKHALAL MAA’AHU AS-SEJNA FATAYNE QAALA AAHADUHUMAA INNEE AARAANEAA AAA’SERU KHAMRAN WA QAALA AL-AAAKHARU INNEE AARAANEAA AAHMELU FAWQA RAASEAA KHUBZAN TAAKULU AT-TAYRU MINHO NABBENAA BETAAWEELEH INNAA NARAAKA MENAL MOHSENEEN.\nNow with him there came into the prison two young men. Said one of them: “I see myself (in a dream) pressing wine.” said the other: “I see myself (in a dream) carrying bread on my head, and birds are eating, thereof.” “Tell us” (they said) “The truth and meaning thereof: for we see thou art one that doth good (to all).” \nقَالَ لَا يَاْتِيْكُمَا طَعَامٌ تُرْزَقٰنِهٖۤ اِلَّا نَبَّاْتُكُمَا بِتَاْوِيْلِهٖ قَبْلَ اَنْ يَّاْتِيَكُمَا ؕ ذٰ لِكُمَا مِمَّا عَلَّمَنِىْ رَبِّىْ ؕ اِنِّىْ تَرَكْتُ مِلَّةَ قَوْمٍ لَّا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَهُمْ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ هُمْ كٰفِرُوْنَ‏(37)\nQAALA LAA YAATEEKUMAA TA-A’AMUN TURZAQAANEH ILLAA NABBAATUKUMAA BETAAWEELEH QABLA AN YYAATEEKUMAA ZAA LEKUMAA MIMMAA A’ALLAMANEAA RABBEE INNEE TARAKTU MILLATA QAWMIN LAA YOAMENOONA BIL-LAAHE WA HUM BIL AAKHERATE HUM KAAFEROON.\nHe said: “Before any food comes (in due course) to feed either of you, I will surely reveal to you the truth and meaning of this ere it befall you: that is part of the (duty) which my Lord hath taught me. I have (I assure you) abandoned the ways of a people that believe not in Allah and that (even) deny the Hereafter. \nوَاتَّبَعْتُ مِلَّةَ اٰبَآءِىْۤ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ وَاِسْحٰقَ وَيَعْقُوْبَؕ مَا كَانَ لَنَاۤ اَنْ نُّشْرِكَ بِاللّٰهِ مِنْ شَىْءٍؕ ذٰلِكَ مِنْ فَضْلِ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْنَا وَعَلَى النَّاسِ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(38)\nWAATTABAA’TU MILLATA AAABAAEAA IBRAAHEEMA WA ISHAAQA WAYAA’QOOBA MAA KAANA LANAA AN NNUSHREKA BIL-LAAHE MIN SHAYIN ZAALEKA MIN FAZLIL LAAHE A’LAYNAA WA NAASE LAAKINNAL AKSARAN NAASE LAA YASHKOROON.\n“And I follow the ways of my fathers, Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob; and never could we attribute any partners whatever to Allah: that (comes) of the grace of Allah to us and to mankind: yet most men are not grateful. \nيٰصَاحِبَىِ السِّجْنِ ءَاَرْبَابٌ مُّتَفَرِّقُوْنَ خَيْرٌ اَمِ اللّٰهُ الْوَاحِدُ الْقَهَّارُؕ‏(39)\nYAASAAHEBAA AS-SEJNE AARBAABUN MMUTAFARREQOONA KHAYRUL AMIL LAAHO AL-WAAHEDU AL-QAHHAARU.\n“O my two companions of the prison! (I ask you): are many lords differing among themselves better, or the One Allah, Supreme and Irresistible? \nمَا تَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِهٖۤ اِلَّاۤ اَسْمَآءً سَمَّيْتُمُوْهَاۤ اَنْتُمْ وَ اٰبَآؤُكُمْ مَّاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ بِهَا مِنْ سُلْطٰنٍؕ اِنِ الْحُكْمُ اِلَّا لِلّٰهِؕ اَمَرَ اَلَّا تَعْبُدُوْۤا اِلَّاۤ اِيَّاهُؕ ذٰلِكَ الدِّيْنُ الْقَيِّمُ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(40)\nMAA TA’BODOONA MIN DOONEHI ILLAA AASMAAAN SAMMAYTUMOOHAA ANTUM WA AAABAAUKUM MAA ANZALAL LAAHO BEHAA MIN SULTAANIN ENIS HUKMO ILLAA LIL-LAAH AMARAL ALLAA TA’BODOO ILLAA AEEAHU ZAALEKAL DEENO AL-QAYMU LAAKINNAL AKSARAN NAASE LAA YA’LAMOON.\n“If not Him, ye worship nothing but names which ye have named, ye and your fathers, for which Allah hath sent down no authority: the command is for none but Allah: He hath commanded that ye worship none but Him: that is the right religion, but most men understand not... \nيٰصَاحِبَىِ السِّجْنِ اَمَّاۤ اَحَدُكُمَا فَيَسْقِىْ رَبَّهٗ خَمْرًاۚ وَاَمَّا الْاٰخَرُ فَيُصْلَبُ فَتَاْكُلُ الطَّيْرُ مِنْ رَّاْسِهٖؕ قُضِىَ الْاَمْرُ الَّذِىْ فِيْهِ تَسْتَفْتِيٰنِؕ‏(41)\nYAASAAHEBAA AS-SEJNE AMMAA AAHADUKUMAA FAYASQEAA WAL KHAMRAN WA AMMAA AL-AAAKHARU FAYUSLABU FATAAKULU AT-TAYRU MIR RRAASEH QUZEAAA MIN LAZEE FEEHE TASTAFTEENE.\n“O my two companions of the prison! As to one of you, he will pour out the wine for his lord to drink: as for the other, he will hang from the cross, and the birds will eat from off his head. (so) hath been decreed that matter whereof ye twain do enquire”... \nوَقَالَ لِلَّذِىْ ظَنَّ اَنَّهٗ نَاجٍ مِّنْهُمَا اذْكُرْنِىْ عِنْدَ رَبِّكَ فَاَنْسٰٮهُ الشَّيْطٰنُ ذِكْرَ رَبِّهٖ فَلَبِثَ فِى السِّجْنِ بِضْعَ سِنِيْنَ‏(42)\nWA QAALA LIL-LAZEE ZANNAS ANNAHU NAAJIN MINHOMAA WA AZKURNEAA I’NDAL RABBEKA FAANSAAHU SHAYTAANO ZEKRA RABBEHI QAWMEHI FIL AS-SEJNE BEZA’A SENEEN.\nAnd of the two, to that one whom he consider about to be saved, he said: “Mention me to thy lord.” But Satan made him forget to mention him to his lord: and (Joseph) lingered in prison a few (more) years. \nوَقَالَ الْمَلِكُ اِنِّىْۤ اَرٰى سَبْعَ بَقَرٰتٍ سِمَانٍ يَّاْكُلُهُنَّ سَبْعٌ عِجَافٌ وَّسَبْعَ سُنْۢبُلٰتٍ خُضْرٍ وَّاُخَرَ يٰبِسٰتٍؕ يٰۤاَيُّهَا الْمَلَاُ اَفْتُوْنِىْ فِىْ رُءْيَاىَ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ لِلرُّءْيَا تَعْبُرُوْنَ‏(43)\nWA QAALA AL-MALEKU INNEE AARAA SAB-A’ BAQARAATIN SEMAANIN YYAAKULUHUNNA SABA’UN E’EJAAFUN WWASABA’A SUNBULAATIN KHUZRINW WWAAKHARA YAABESAATIN YAA-AYYOHAL MALA-O AFTOONEE FEE RUYAAAAA IN KUNTUM LELRRUYAA TAA’BUROONA.\nThe king (of Egypt) said: “I do see (in a vision) seven fat kine, whom seven lean ones devour, and seven green ears of corn, and seven (others) withered. O ye chiefs! Expound to me my vision if it be that ye can interpret visions.” \nقَالُوْۤا اَضْغَاثُ اَحْلَامٍۚ وَمَا نَحْنُ بِتَاْوِيْلِ الْاَحْلَامِ بِعٰلِمِيْنَ‏(44)\nQAALOO AAZGHAASU AAHLAAMIN WA MAA NAHNO BETAAWEELE AL-AAHLAAME BEA’AALEMEENA.\nThey said: “A confused medley of dreams: and we are not skilled in the interpretation of dreams.” \nوَقَالَ الَّذِىْ نَجَا مِنْهُمَا وَادَّكَرَ بَعْدَ اُمَّةٍ اَنَا اُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِتَاْوِيْلِهٖ فَاَرْسِلُوْنِ‏(45)\nWA QAALA LAZEE NAJAA MINHOMAA WAADDAKARA BA’DA UMMATIN ANAA AUNABBEUKUM BETAAWEELEH FAARSELOONE.\nBut the man who had been released, one of the two (who had been in prison) and who now bethought him after (so long) a space of time, said: “I will tell you the truth of its interpretation: send ye me (therefore).” \nيُوْسُفُ اَيُّهَا الصِّدِّيْقُ اَ فْتِنَا فِىْ سَبْعِ بَقَرٰتٍ سِمَانٍ يَّاْكُلُهُنَّ سَبْعٌ عِجَافٌ وَّسَبْعِ سُنْۢبُلٰتٍ خُضْرٍ وَّاُخَرَ يٰبِسٰتٍ ۙ لَّعَلِّىْۤ اَرْجِعُ اِلَى النَّاسِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(46)\nYOOSUFU AYYOHAL AS-SEDDEEQU AAFTENAA FEE SABE’E BAQARAATIN SEMAANIN YYAAKULUHUNNA SABA’UN E’EJAAFUN WWASABE’E SUNBULAATIN KHUZRINW WWAAKHARA YAABESAATIN LA-A’LLEE AARJEU’U ELAL NAASE LA-A’LLAHUM YA’LAMOON.\n“O Joseph!” (he said) “O man of truth! Expound to us (the dream) of seven fat kine whom seven lean ones devour, and of seven green ears of corn and (seven) others withered: that I may return to the people, and that they may understand.” \nقَالَ تَزْرَعُوْنَ سَبْعَ سِنِيْنَ دَاَبًاۚ فَمَا حَصَدْتُّمْ فَذَرُوْهُ فِىْ سُنْۢبُلِهٖۤ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا مِّمَّا تَاْكُلُوْنَ‏(47)\nQAALA TAZRAU’OONA SAB-A’ SENEEN DAABAN FAMAA HASADTTUM FAZAROOHU FEE SUNBULEH ILLAA QALEELAA MIMMAA TAAKULOONA.\n(Joseph) said: “For seven years shall ye diligently sow as is your wont: and the harvests that ye reap, ye shall leave them in the ear, except a little, of which ye shall eat. \nثُمَّ يَاْتِىْ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ ذٰلِكَ سَبْعٌ شِدَادٌ يَّاْكُلْنَ مَا قَدَّمْتُمْ لَهُنَّ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا مِّمَّا تُحْصِنُوْنَ‏(48)\nSUMMA YAATEE MIN BA’DE ZAALEKA SABA’UN SHEDAADUN YYAAKULNA MAA QADDAMTUM LAHUNNA ILLAA QALEELAA MIMMAA TUHSENOONA.\n“Then will come after that (period) seven dreadful (years), which will devour what ye shall have laid by in advance for them, (all) except a little which ye shall have (specially) guarded. \nثُمَّ يَاْتِىْ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ ذٰلِكَ عَامٌ فِيْهِ يُغَاثُ النَّاسُ وَفِيْهِ يَعْصِرُوْنَ‏(49)\nSUMMA YAATEE MIN BA’DE ZAALEKA A’AAMUN FEEHE YUGHAASU NAASO WA FEEHE YAA’SEROONA.\n“Then will come after that (period) a year in which the people will have abundant water, and in which they will press (wine and oil).” \nوَقَالَ الْمَلِكُ ائْتُوْنِىْ بِهٖۚ فَلَمَّا جَآءَهُ الرَّسُوْلُ قَالَ ارْجِعْ اِلٰى رَبِّكَ فَسْئَلْهُ مَا بَالُ النِّسْوَةِ الّٰتِىْ قَطَّعْنَ اَيْدِيَهُنَّؕ اِنَّ رَبِّىْ بِكَيْدِهِنَّ عَلِيْمٌ‏(50)\nWA QAALA AL-MALEKU ATOONEAA BEHI FALAMMAA JAAA-AHUL RASOOLO QAALA ARJEA’ ELAA RABBEKA FASALHU MAA BAALU AN-NESWATE KHAALEKA QATTAA’NA AAYDEEHUNNA INNAL RABBEE BEKAYDEHENNA A’LEEM.\nSo the king said: “Bring ye him unto me.” But when the messenger came to him, (Joseph) said: “Go thou back to thy lord, and ask him, 'What is the state of mind of the ladies who cut their hands'? For my Lord is certainly well aware of their snare.” \nقَالَ مَا خَطْبُكُنَّ اِذْ رَاوَدْتُّنَّ يُوْسُفَ عَنْ نَّفْسِهٖؕ قُلْنَ حَاشَ لِلّٰهِ مَا عَلِمْنَا عَلَيْهِ مِنْ سُوْۤءٍ ؕ قَالَتِ امْرَاَتُ الْعَزِيْزِ الْئٰنَ حَصْحَصَ الْحَقُّ اَنَا رَاوَدْتُّهٗ عَنْ نَّفْسِهٖ وَاِنَّهٗ لَمِنَ الصّٰدِقِيْنَ‏(51)\nQAALA MAA KHATBUKUNNA IZ RAAWADTTUNNA YOOSUFA A’N NNAFSEH QULNA HAASHA LILLAAHE MAA A’LIMNAA A’LAYHE MIN SOOIN QAALATE AMRAATU A’ZEEZIL AL-AANA HASHASA HAQQO ANAA RAAWADTTUH A’N NNAFSEH WA INNAHU LAMENAS SAADEQEENA.\n(The king) said (to the ladies): “What was your affair when ye did seek to seduce Joseph from his (true) self?” The ladies said: “Allah preserve us! no evil know we against him!” Said the 'Aziz's wife: “Now is the truth manifest (to all): it was I who sought to seduce him from his (true) self: He is indeed of those who are (ever) true (and virtuous). \nذٰ لِكَ لِيَعْلَمَ اَنِّىْ لَمْ اَخُنْهُ بِالْغَيْبِ وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَهْدِىْ كَيْدَ الْخَآئِنِيْنَ‏(52)\nZAA LEKA LEEA’LAMA AANNEAA LAM AAKHUNHU BIL-GHAYBE WA ANNAL LAAHA LAA YAHDEE KAYDA AL-KHAAENEENA.\n“This (say I), in order that He may know that I have never been false to him in his absence, and that Allah will never guide the snare of the false ones. \nوَمَاۤ اُبَرِّئُ نَفْسِىْۚ اِنَّ النَّفْسَ لَاَمَّارَةٌۢ بِالسُّوْٓءِ اِلَّا مَا رَحِمَ رَبِّىْ ؕاِنَّ رَبِّىْ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(53)\nWA MAA AUBARREU NAFSEE INNAL AN-NAFSA LAAMMAARATUN BIS-SOOO-E ILLAA MAA RAHEMA RABBEE AENNA RABBEE GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\n“Nor do I absolve my own self (of blame): the (human) soul is certainly prone to evil, unless my Lord do bestow His Mercy: but surely my Lord is Oft-forgiving, Most Merciful.” \nوَقَالَ الْمَلِكُ ائْتُوْنِىْ بِهٖۤ اَسْتَخْلِصْهُ لِنَفْسِىْۚ فَلَمَّا كَلَّمَهٗ قَالَ اِنَّكَ الْيَوْمَ لَدَيْنَا مَكِيْنٌ اَمِيْنٌ‏(54)\nWA QAALA AL-MALEKU ATOONEAA BEHI AASTAKHLESHU LE-NAFSEE FALAMMAA KALLAMAH QAALA INNAKA YAWMA LADAYNAA MAKEENUN AMEEN.\nSo the king said: “Bring him unto me; I will take him specially to serve about my own person.” Therefore when he had spoken to him, he said: “Be assured this day, thou art, before our own presence, with rank firmly established, and fidelity fully proved! \nقَالَ اجْعَلْنِىْ عَلٰى خَزَآئِنِ الْاَرْضِۚ اِنِّىْ حَفِيْظٌ عَلِيْمٌ‏(55)\nQAALA AJA’ALNEAA A’LAA KHAZAAENE ARZE INNEE HAFEEZUN A’LEEM.\n(Joseph) said: “Set me over the store-houses of the land: I will indeed guard them, as one that knows (their importance).” \nوَكَذٰلِكَ مَكَّنَّا لِيُوْسُفَ فِى الْاَرْضِۚ يَتَبَوَّاُ مِنْهَا حَيْثُ يَشَآءُ ؕ نُصِيْبُ بِرَحْمَتِنَا مَنْ نَّشَآءُۚ وَلَا نُضِيْعُ اَجْرَ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(56)\nWA KAZAALEKA MAKKANNAA LEEWSUFA FIL ARZE YATABAWAU MINHAA HAYSO YASHAAA NUSEEBU BERAHMATENAA MAN NNASHAAU WA LAA NUZEEU’U AJRA MOHSENEEN.\nThus did We give established power to Joseph in the land, to take possession therein as, when, or where he pleased. We bestow of our Mercy on whom We please, and We suffer not, to be lost, the reward of those who do good. \nوَلَاَجْرُ الْاٰخِرَةِ خَيْرٌ لِّلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَكَانُوْا يَتَّقُوْنَ‏(57)\nWALAAJRU AAKHERATE KHAYRUL LIL-LAZEENA AAMANOO WA KAANOO YATTAQOON.\nBut verily the reward of the Hereafter is the best, for those who believe, and are constant in righteousness. \nوَجَآءَ اِخْوَةُ يُوْسُفَ فَدَخَلُوْا عَلَيْهِ فَعَرَفَهُمْ وَهُمْ لَهٗ مُنْكِرُوْنَ‏(58)\nWA JAAA-A AEKHWATU YOOSUFA FA DAKHALOO A’LAYHE FAA’ARAFAHUM WA HUM LAHU MUNKEROONA.\nThen came Joseph's brethren: they entered his presence, and he knew them, but they knew him not. \nوَ لَمَّا جَهَّزَهُمْ بِجَهَازِهِمْ قَالَ ائْتُوْنِىْ بِاَخٍ لَّكُمْ مِّنْ اَبِيْكُمْۚ اَلَا تَرَوْنَ اَنِّىْۤ اُوْفِی الْكَيْلَ وَاَنَا خَيْرُ الْمُنْزِلِيْنَ‏(59)\nWA LAMMAA JAHHAZAHUM BEJAHAAZEHEM QAALA ATOONEAA BEAAKHIN LAKUM MIN AABEEKUM ALAA TARAWNA AANNEAA AOOFEE AL-KAYLA ANAT KHAYRUR AL-MUNZELEENA.\nAnd when he had furnished them forth with provisions (suitable) for them, he said: “Bring unto me a brother ye have, of the same father as yourselves, (but a different mother): see ye not that I pay out full measure, and that I do provide the best hospitality? \nفَاِنْ لَّمْ تَاْتُوْنِىْ بِهٖ فَلَا كَيْلَ لَكُمْ عِنْدِىْ وَلَا تَقْرَبُوْنِ‏(60)\nFA-IN LAM TAATOONEAA BEHI FALAA KAYLA LAKUM E’ENDEAA WA LAA TAQRABOONE.\n“Now if ye bring him not to me, ye shall have no measure (of corn) from me, nor shall ye (even) come near me.” \nقَالُوْا سَنُرَاوِدُ عَنْهُ اَبَاهُ وَاِنَّا لَفَاعِلُوْنَ‏(61)\nQAALOO SANURAAWEDU A’NHO AABAAHU WA INNAA LAFAAE’ELOONA.\nThey said: “We shall certainly seek to get our wish about him from his father: Indeed we shall do it.” \nوَقَالَ لِفِتْيٰنِهِ اجْعَلُوْا بِضَاعَتَهُمْ فِىْ رِحَالِهِمْ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَعْرِفُوْنَهَاۤ اِذَا انْقَلَبُوْۤا اِلٰٓى اَهْلِهِمْ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَرْجِعُوْنَ‏(62)\nWA QAALA LEFETYAANEHE AJA’ALOOA BEZAAA’ATAHUM FEE REHAALEHEM LA-A’LLAHUM YAA’REFOONAHAA EZAA QALABOO ELAA AHLEHIM LA-A’LLAHUM YARJE-O’ON.\nAnd (Joseph) told his servants to put their stock-in-trade (with which they had bartered) into their saddle-bags, so they should know it only when they returned to their people, in order that they might come back. \nفَلَمَّا رَجَعُوْۤا اِلٰٓى اَبِيْهِمْ قَالُوْا يٰۤاَبَانَا مُنِعَ مِنَّا الْكَيْلُ فَاَرْسِلْ مَعَنَاۤ اَخَانَا نَكْتَلْ وَاِنَّا لَهٗ لَحٰفِظُوْنَ‏(63)\nFALAMMAA RAJAU’OOA ELAA AABEEHEM QAALOO YAABAANAA MUNEA’A MINNAA AL-KAYLU FAARSEL MAA’ANAA AAKHAANAA NAKTAL WA INNAA LAHU LAHAAFEZOONA.\nNow when they returned to their father, they said: “O our father! No more measure of grain shall we get (unless we take our brother): So send our brother with us, that we may get our measure; and we will indeed take every care of him.” \nقَالَ هَلْ اٰمَنُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ اِلَّا كَمَاۤ اَمِنْتُكُمْ عَلٰٓى اَخِيْهِ مِنْ قَبْلُؕ فَاللّٰهُ خَيْرٌ حٰفِظًا وَّهُوَ اَرْحَمُ الرّٰحِمِيْنَ‏(64)\nQAALA HAL AAAMANUKUM A’LAYHE ILLAA KAMAA AAMENTUKUM A’LAA AKHEEHE MIN QABL WA FAL-LAAHO KHAYRUL HAAFEZAN WA AARHAMU AR-RAAHEMEENA.\nHe said: “Shall I trust you with him with any result other than when I trusted you with his brother aforetime? But Allah is the best to take care (of him), and He is the Most Merciful of those who show mercy!” \nوَلَمَّا فَتَحُوْا مَتَاعَهُمْ وَجَدُوْا بِضَاعَتَهُمْ رُدَّتْ اِلَيْهِمْؕ قَالُوْا يٰۤاَبَانَا مَا نَبْغِىْؕ هٰذِهٖ بِضَاعَتُنَا رُدَّتْ اِلَيْنَا ۚ وَنَمِيْرُ اَهْلَنَا وَنَحْفَظُ اَخَانَا وَنَزْدَادُ كَيْلَ بَعِيْرٍؕ ذٰ لِكَ كَيْلٌ يَّسِيْرٌ‏(65)\nWA LAMMAA FATAHOOA MATAAA’AHUM WAJADOOA BEZAAA’ATAHUM RUDDAT AELAYHEM QAALOO YAABAANAA MAA NABGHEAA HAAZEHI BEZAAA’ATUNAA RUDDAT ELAYNAA WANAMEERU AAHLANAA WANAHFAZU AAKHAANAA WANAZDAADU KAYLA BAE’EERIN ZAA LEKA KAYLUN YYASEERUN.\nThen when they opened their baggage, they found their stock-in-trade had been returned to them. They said: “O our father! What (more) can we desire? this our stock-in-trade has been returned to us: so we shall get (more) food for our family; We shall take care of our brother; and add (at the same time) a full camel's load (of grain to our provisions). This is but a small quantity. \nقَالَ لَنْ اُرْسِلَهٗ مَعَكُمْ حَتّٰى تُؤْتُوْنِ مَوْثِقًا مِّنَ اللّٰهِ لَتَاْتُنَّنِىْ بِهٖۤ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يُّحَاطَ بِكُمْۚ فَلَمَّاۤ اٰتَوْهُ مَوْثِقَهُمْ قَالَ اللّٰهُ عَلٰى مَا نَقُوْلُ وَكِيْلٌ‏(66)\nQAALA LAN AURSELAH MA-A’KUM HATTAA TUTOONE MAWSEQAN MENAL LAAHE LATAATUNNANEAA BEHI ILLAA AN YYUHAATA BEKUM FALAMMAA AAATAWHU MAWSEQAHUM QAALAL LAAHO A’LAA MAA NAQOOLU WAKEELUN.\n(Jacob) said: “Never will I send him with you until ye swear a solemn oath to me, in Allah's name, that ye will be sure to bring him back to me unless ye are yourselves hemmed in (and made powerless). And when they had sworn their solemn oath, he said: “Over all that we say, be Allah the witness and guardian!” \nوَقَالَ يٰبَنِىَّ لَا تَدْخُلُوْا مِنْۢ بَابٍ وَّاحِدٍ وَّادْخُلُوْا مِنْ اَبْوَابٍ مُّتَفَرِّقَةٍؕ وَمَاۤ اُغْنِىْ عَنْكُمْ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ مِنْ شَىْءٍؕ اِنِ الْحُكْمُ اِلَّا لِلّٰهِؕ عَلَيْهِ تَوَكَّلْتُۚ وَعَلَيْهِ فَلْيَتَوَكَّلِ الْمُتَوَكِّلُوْنَ‏(67)\nWA QAALA BANIYYA LAA LAA MIN BAABIN WAAHEDIN WWAADKHULOOA MIN AABWAABIN MMUTAFARREQATIN WA MAA AUGHNEAA A’NKUM MENAL LAAHE MIN SHAYIN ENIS HUKMO ILLAA LIL-LAAH A’LAYHE TAWAKKALTU WA A’LAYHE FALYATAWAKKALE AL-MUTAWAKKELOONA.\nFurther he said: “O my sons! enter not all by one gate: enter ye by different gates. Not that I can profit you aught against Allah (with my advice): None can command except Allah: On Him do I put my trust: and let all that trust put their trust on Him.” \nوَلَمَّا دَخَلُوْا مِنْ حَيْثُ اَمَرَهُمْ اَبُوْهُمْ ؕمَا كَانَ يُغْنِىْ عَنْهُمْ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ مِنْ شَىْءٍ اِلَّا حَاجَةً فِىْ نَفْسِ يَعْقُوْبَ قَضٰٮهَاؕ وَاِنَّهٗ لَذُوْ عِلْمٍ لِّمَا عَلَّمْنٰهُ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(68)\nWA LAMMAA DAKHALOO MIN HAYSO AAMARAHUM AABOOHUM MAA KAANA YUGHNEE A’NHUM MENAL LAAHE MIN SHAY-IN ILLAA HAAJATAM FEE NAFSE YA’QOOBAL QAZAAHAA WA INNAHU LAZOO I’LMIN LEMAA A’LLAMNAAHUSH-SHE’RA LAAKINNAL AKSARAN NAASE LAA YA’LAMOON.\nAnd when they entered in the manner their father had enjoined, it did not profit them in the least against (the plan of) Allah: It was but a necessity of Jacob's soul, which he discharged. For he was, by our instruction, full of knowledge (and experience): but most men know not. \nوَلَمَّا دَخَلُوْا عَلٰى يُوْسُفَ اٰوٰٓى اِلَيْهِ اَخَاهُ قَالَ اِنِّىْۤ اَنَا اَخُوْكَ فَلَا تَبْتَئِسْ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(69)\nWA LAMMAA DAKHALOO A’LAA YOOSUFA AAAWAAA ELAYHE AAKHAAHU QAALA INNEE ANAA AAKHOOKA FALAA TABTAES BEMAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nNow when they came into Joseph's presence, he received his (full) brother to stay with him. He said (to him): “Behold! I am thy (own) brother; so grieve not at aught of their doings.” \nفَلَمَّا جَهَّزَهُمْ بِجَهَازِهِمْ جَعَلَ السِّقَايَةَ فِىْ رَحْلِ اَخِيْهِ ثُمَّ اَذَّنَ مُؤَذِّنٌ اَ يَّتُهَا الْعِيْرُ اِنَّكُمْ لَسَارِقُوْنَ‏(70)\nFALAMMAA JAHHAZAHUM BEJAHAAZEHEM JA-A’LAL AS-SEQAAYATA FEE RAHLE AKHEEHE SUMMA AAZZANA MUAZZENUN AAYTUHAA AL-E’EERU INNAKUM LASAAREQOONA.\nAt length when he had furnished them forth with provisions (suitable) for them, he put the drinking cup into his brother's saddle-bag. Then shouted out a crier: “O ye (in) the caravan! behold! ye are thieves, without doubt!” \nقَالُوْا وَاَقْبَلُوْا عَلَيْهِمْ مَّاذَا تَفْقِدُوْنَ‏(71)\nQAALOO WAAQBALOOA A’LAYHIM MMAAZAA TAFQEDOONA.\nThey said, turning towards them: “What is it that ye miss?” \nقَالُوْا نَفْقِدُ صُوَاعَ الْمَلِكِ وَلِمَنْ جَآءَ بِهٖ حِمْلُ بَعِيْرٍ وَّاَنَا بِهٖ زَعِيْمٌ‏(72)\nQAALOO NAFQEDU SOOAA’A MALEKIL WA LEMAN JAAA-A BEHI HEMLU BAE’EERIN WWAANAA BEHI ZAE’EEMUN.\nThey said: “We miss the great beaker of the king; for him who produces it, is (the reward of) a camel load; I will be bound by it.” \nقَالُوْا تَاللّٰهِ لَقَدْ عَلِمْتُمْ مَّا جِئْنَا لِنُفْسِدَ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَمَا كُنَّا سَارِقِيْنَ‏(73)\nQAALOO TAALLLAAHE LAQAD A’ALEMTUM MAA JENAA LENUFSEDA FIL ARZE WA MAA KUNNAA SAAREQEENA.\n(The brothers) said: “By Allah! well ye know that we came not to make mischief in the land, and we are no thieves!” \nقَالُوْا فَمَا جَزَاۤؤُهٗۤ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ كٰذِبِيْنَ‏(74)\nQAALOO FAMAA JAZAAUH IN KUNTUM KAAZEBEENA.\n(The Egyptians) said: “What then shall be the penalty of this, if ye are (proved) to have lied?” \nقَالُوْا جَزَاۤؤُهٗ مَنْ وُّجِدَ فِىْ رَحْلِهٖ فَهُوَ جَزَاۤؤُهٗؕ كَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(75)\nQAALOO JAZAAUH MAN WWUJEDA FEE RAHLEH FAHOWA JAZAAUH KAZAALEKA NAJZIL ZAALEMEEN.\nThey said: “The penalty should be that he in whose saddle-bag it is found, should be held (as bondman) to atone for the (crime). Thus it is we punish the wrong-doers!” \nفَبَدَاَ بِاَوْعِيَتِهِمْ قَبْلَ وِعَآءِ اَخِيْهِ ثُمَّ اسْتَخْرَجَهَا مِنْ وِّعَآءِ اَخِيْهِؕ كَذٰلِكَ كِدْنَا لِيُوْسُفَؕ مَا كَانَ لِيَاْخُذَ اَخَاهُ فِىْ دِيْنِ الْمَلِكِ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يَّشَآءَ اللّٰهُؕ نَرْفَعُ دَرَجٰتٍ مَّنْ نَّشَآءُؕ وَفَوْقَ كُلِّ ذِىْ عِلْمٍ عَلِيْمٌ‏(76)\nFABADAABEAAWE’EETEHEM QABLA WEA’AAE AKHEEHE SUMMA ASTAKHRAJAHAA MIN WWEA’AAE AAKHEEHE KAZAALEKA KEDNAA LEEWSUFA MAA KAANA LEEAKHUZA AAKHAAHU FEE DEEN MALEKIL ILLAA AN YASHAAA-ALLAAH NARFAU’U DARAJAATIN MAN NNASHAAU WA FAWQA KULLE ZEE I’LMIN A’LEEM.\nSo he began (the search) with their baggage, before (he came to) the baggage of his brother: at length he brought it out of his brother's baggage. Thus did We plan for Joseph. He could not take his brother by the law of the king except that Allah willed it (so). We raise to degrees (of wisdom) whom We please: but over all endued with knowledge is one, the All-Knowing. \nقَالُوْۤا اِنْ يَّسْرِقْ فَقَدْ سَرَقَ اَخٌ لَّهٗ مِنْ قَبْلُ ۚ فَاَسَرَّهَا يُوْسُفُ فِىْ نَفْسِهٖ وَلَمْ يُبْدِهَا لَهُمْ ۚ قَالَ اَنْتُمْ شَرٌّ مَّكَانًا ۚ وَاللّٰهُ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا تَصِفُوْنَ‏(77)\nQAALOO IN YYASREQ FAQAD SARAQA AAKHUN LAHU MIN QABLO FAASARRAHAA YOOSUFU FEE WA WA LAM YUBDEHAA LAHUM QAALA ANTUM HOWA MMAKAANAN WAL LAAHO A-A’LAMO BEMAA TASEFOONA.\nThey said: “If he steals, there was a brother of his who did steal before (him).” But these things did Joseph keep locked in his heart, revealing not the secrets to them. He (simply) said (to himself): “Ye are the worse situated; and Allah knoweth best the truth of what ye assert!” \nقَالُوْا يٰۤاَيُّهَا الْعَزِيْزُ اِنَّ لَهٗۤ اَبًا شَيْخًا كَبِيْرًا فَخُذْ اَحَدَنَا مَكَانَهٗۚ اِنَّا نَرٰٮكَ مِنَ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(78)\nQAALOO YAA-AYYOHAL A’ZEEZUL INNAL LAHU AABAN SHAYKHAN KABEERAA FA-KHUZ AAHADANAA MAKAANAHU INNAA NARAAKA MENAL MOHSENEEN.\nThey said: “O exalted one! Behold! he has a father, aged and venerable, (who will grieve for him); so take one of us in his place; for we see that thou art (gracious) in doing good.” \nقَالَ مَعَاذَ اللّٰهِ اَنْ نَّاْخُذَ اِلَّا مَنْ وَّجَدْنَا مَتَاعَنَا عِنْدَهٗۤ ۙ اِنَّاۤ اِذًا لَّظٰلِمُوْنَ‏(79)\nQAALA MAA’AAZA LAAHE AN NNAAKHUZA ILLAA MAN WWAJADNAA MATAAA’ANAA I’NDAHU INNAA EZAL LLAZAALEMOONA.\nHe said: “Allah forbid that we take other than him with whom we found our property: indeed (if we did so), we should be acting wrongfully. \nفَلَمَّا اسْتَايْئَسُوْا مِنْهُ خَلَصُوْا نَجِيًّا ؕ قَالَ كَبِيْرُهُمْ اَلَمْ تَعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّ اَبَاكُمْ قَدْ اَخَذَ عَلَيْكُمْ مَّوْثِقًا مِّنَ اللّٰهِ وَمِنْ قَبْلُ مَا فَرَّطْتُّمْ فِىْ يُوْسُفَ ۚ فَلَنْ اَبْرَحَ الْاَرْضَ حَتّٰى يَاْذَنَ لِىْۤ اَبِىْۤ اَوْ يَحْكُمَ اللّٰهُ لِىْ ۚ وَهُوَ خَيْرُ الْحٰكِمِيْنَ‏(80)\nFALAMMAA ASTAAYASOOA MINHO KHALASOOA NAJEEA QAALA KABEERUHUM ALAM TA’LAMOO ANNAL AABAAKUM QAD AAKHAZA A’LAYKUM MMAWSEQAN MENAL LAAHE WA MIN QABLO MAA FARRATTUM FEE YOOSUFA FALAN AABRAHA ARZA HATTAA YAAZANA LEE ABEE AW YAHKUMA LAAHO LEE WA HOWA KHAYRUR HAAKEMEEN.\nNow when they saw no hope of his (yielding), they held a conference in private. The leader among them said: “Know ye not that your father did take an oath from you in Allah's name, and how, before this, ye did fail in your duty with Joseph? Therefore will I not leave this land until my father permits me, or Allah commands me; and He is the best to command. \nاِرْجِعُوْۤا اِلٰٓى اَبِيْكُمْ فَقُوْلُوْا يٰۤاَبَانَاۤ اِنَّ ابْنَكَ سَرَقَۚ وَمَا شَهِدْنَاۤ اِلَّا بِمَا عَلِمْنَا وَمَا كُنَّا لِلْغَيْبِ حٰفِظِيْنَ‏(81)\nAERJEU’OOA ELAA AABEEKUM FAQOOLOOA YAABAANAA INNA ABNAKA SARAQA WA MAA SHAHIDNAA ILLAA BEMAA A’LIMNAA WA MAA KUNNAA LIL-GHAYBE HAAFEZEEN.\n“Turn ye back to your father, and say, 'O our father! behold! thy son committed theft! we bear witness only to what we know, and we could not well guard against the unseen! \nوَسْئَلِ الْقَرْيَةَ الَّتِىْ كُنَّا فِيْهَا وَالْعِيْرَ الَّتِىْ اَقْبَلْنَا فِيْهَاؕ وَاِنَّا لَصٰدِقُوْنَ‏(82)\nWASALE QARYATA LATEE KUNNAA FEEHAA WAL E’EERA LATEE AAQBALNAA FEEHAA WA INNAA LASAADEQOON.\n“'Ask at the town where we have been and the caravan in which we returned, and (you will find) we are indeed telling the truth.'“ \nقَالَ بَلْ سَوَّلَتْ لَكُمْ اَنْفُسُكُمْ اَمْرًاؕ فَصَبْرٌ جَمِيْلٌؕ عَسَى اللّٰهُ اَنْ يَّاْتِيَنِىْ بِهِمْ جَمِيْعًاؕ اِنَّهٗ هُوَ الْعَلِيْمُ الْحَكِيْمُ‏(83)\nQAALA BAL SAWLAT LAKUM ANFOSOKUM AAMRAN FASABRUN JAMEELUN A’ASAA LAAHO AN YYAATEENEAA BEHIM JAMEEA’AN INNAHU HOWA A’LEEM HAKEEM.\nJacob said: “Nay, but ye have yourselves contrived a story (good enough) for you. So patience is most fitting (for me). Maybe Allah will bring them (back) all to me (in the end). For He is indeed full of knowledge and wisdom.” \nوَتَوَلّٰى عَنْهُمْ وَقَالَ يٰۤاَسَفٰى عَلٰى يُوْسُفَ وَابْيَضَّتْ عَيْنٰهُ مِنَ الْحُزْنِ فَهُوَ كَظِيْمٌ‏(84)\nWA TAWALLAA A’NHUM WA QAALA YAASAFAA A’LAA YOOSUFA WAABYAZZAT A’AYNAAHU MENAL AL-HUZNE FAHOWA KAZEEMUN.\nAnd he turned away from them, and said: “How great is my grief for Joseph!” And his eyes became white with sorrow, and he fell into silent melancholy. \nقَالُوْا تَاللّٰهِ تَفْتَؤُا تَذْكُرُ يُوْسُفَ حَتّٰى تَكُوْنَ حَرَضًا اَوْ تَكُوْنَ مِنَ الْهَالِكِيْنَ‏(85)\nQAALOO TAALLLAAHE TAFTAUA TAZKURU YOOSUFA HATTAA TAKOONA HARAZAN AW TAKOONA MENAL AL-HAALEKEENA.\nThey said: “By Allah! (never) wilt thou cease to remember Joseph until thou reach the last extremity of illness, or until thou die!” \nقَالَ اِنَّمَاۤ اَشْكُوْا بَثِّىْ وَحُزْنِىْۤ اِلَى اللّٰهِ وَاَعْلَمُ مِنَ اللّٰهِ مَا لَا تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(86)\nQAALA INNAMAA AASHKOOA BASSEAA WAHUZNEAA ELAL LAAHE WA A-A’LAMO MENAL LAAHE MAA LAA TA’LAMOON.\nHe said: “I only complain of my distraction and anguish to Allah, and I know from Allah that which ye know not... \nيٰبَنِىَّ اذْهَبُوْا فَتَحَسَّسُوْا مِنْ يُّوْسُفَ وَاَخِيْهِ وَلَا تَايْئَسُوْا مِنْ رَّوْحِ اللّٰهِؕ اِنَّهٗ لَا يَايْئَسُ مِنْ رَّوْحِ اللّٰهِ اِلَّا الْقَوْمُ الْكٰفِرُوْنَ‏(87)\nBANIYYA AZHABOOA FATAHASSASOOA MIN YYOOSUFA WA AKHEEHE WA LAA TAAYASOOA MIR RRAWHE LAAH INNAHU LAA YAAYASU MIR RRAWHE LAAHE ILLAL AL-QAWMU KAAFEROON.\n“O my sons! go ye and enquire about Joseph and his brother, and never give up hope of Allah's Soothing Mercy: truly no one despairs of Allah's Soothing Mercy, except those who have no faith.” \nفَلَمَّا دَخَلُوْا عَلَيْهِ قَالُوْا يٰۤاَيُّهَا الْعَزِيْزُ مَسَّنَا وَاَهْلَنَا الضُّرُّ وَجِئْنَا بِبِضَاعَةٍ مُّزْجٰٮةٍ فَاَوْفِ لَنَا الْكَيْلَ وَتَصَدَّقْ عَلَيْنَاؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَجْزِى الْمُتَصَدِّقِيْنَ‏(88)\nFALAMMAA DAKHALOO A’LAYHE QAALOO YAA-AYYOHAL A’ZEEZUL MASSANAA WAAHLANAA AZ-ZURRU WAJENAA BEBEZAAA’ATIN MMUZJAATIN FAAWFE LANAA AL-KAYLA WATASADDAQ A’ALAYNAA INNAL LAAHA YAJZEAA AL-MUTASADDEQEENA.\nThen, when they came (back) into (Joseph's) presence they said: “O exalted one! distress has seized us and our family: we have (now) brought but scanty capital: so pay us full measure, (we pray thee), and treat it as charity to us: for Allah doth reward the charitable.” \nقَالَ هَلْ عَلِمْتُمْ مَّا فَعَلْتُمْ بِيُوْسُفَ وَاَخِيْهِ اِذْ اَنْتُمْ جٰهِلُوْنَ‏(89)\nQAALA HAL A’ALEMTUM MAA FAA’ALTUM BEEWSUFA WA AKHEEHE IZ ANTUM JAAHELOONA.\nHe said: “Know ye how ye dealt with Joseph and his brother, not knowing (what ye were doing)?” \nقَالُوْۤا ءَاِنَّكَ لَاَنْتَ يُوْسُفُؕ قَالَ اَنَا يُوْسُفُ وَهٰذَاۤ اَخِىْ قَدْ مَنَّ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْنَاؕ اِنَّهٗ مَنْ يَّتَّقِ وَيَصْبِرْ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يُضِيْعُ اَجْرَ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(90)\nQAALOO AANNAKA LAANTA YOOSUFU QAALA ANAA YOOSUFU WA AAKHEAA QAD MANNA LAAHO A’ALAYNAA INNAHU MAN YATTAQIL WAYASBER FA-INNAL LAAHA LAA YUZEEU’U AJRA MOHSENEEN.\nThey said: “Art thou indeed Joseph?” He said, “I am Joseph, and this is my brother: Allah has indeed been gracious to us (all): behold, he that is righteous and patient, never will Allah suffer the reward to be lost, of those who do right.” \nقَالُوْا تَاللّٰهِ لَقَدْ اٰثَرَكَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْنَا وَاِنْ كُنَّا لَخٰطِئِيْنَ‏(91)\nQAALOO TAALLLAAHE LAQAD AAASARAKA LAAHO A’LAYNAA WA KUNNAA LAKHAATEEENA.\nThey said: “By Allah! indeed has Allah preferred thee above us, and we certainly have been guilty of sin!” \nقَالَ لَا تَثْرِيْبَ عَلَيْكُمُ الْيَوْمَؕ يَغْفِرُ اللّٰهُ لَكُمْ وَهُوَ اَرْحَمُ الرّٰحِمِيْنَ‏(92)\nQAALA LAA TASREEBA A’LAYKOMUL AL-YAWMA YAGHFERO LAAHO LAKUM WA HOWA AARHAMU AR-RAAHEMEENA.\nHe said: “This day let no reproach be (cast) on you: Allah will forgive you, and He is the Most Merciful of those who show mercy! \nاِذْهَبُوْا بِقَمِيْصِىْ هٰذَا فَاَلْقُوْهُ عَلٰى وَجْهِ اَبِىْ يَاْتِ بَصِيْرًاۚ وَاْتُوْنِىْ بِاَهْلِكُمْ اَجْمَعِيْنَ‏(93)\nAEZHABOOA BEQAMEESEAA HAAZAA FAALQOOHU A’LAA WAJHIL ABEE TAKOONOO BASEERAA WAATOONEE BEAAHLEKUM AJMA-E’ENA.\n“Go with this my shirt, and cast it over the face of my father: he will come to see (clearly). Then come ye (here) to me together with all your family.” \nوَلَمَّا فَصَلَتِ الْعِيْرُ قَالَ اَبُوْهُمْ اِنِّىْ لَاَجِدُ رِيْحَ يُوْسُفَ لَوْلَاۤ اَنْ تُفَنِّدُوْنِ‏(94)\nWA LAMMAA FASALATE AL-E’EERU QAALA AABOOHUM INNEE LAAJEDU REEHA YOOSUFA LAWLAA AN TUFANNEDOONE.\nWhen the caravan left (Egypt), their father said: “I do indeed scent the presence of Joseph: Nay, think me not a dotard.” \nقَالُوْا تَاللّٰهِ اِنَّكَ لَفِىْ ضَلٰلِكَ الْقَدِيْمِ‏(95)\nQAALOO TAALLLAAHE INNAKA LAFEE ZALAALEKA QADEEM.\nThey said: “By Allah! truly thou art in thine old wandering mind.” \nفَلَمَّاۤ اَنْ جَآءَ الْبَشِيْرُ اَلْقٰٮهُ عَلٰى وَجْهِهٖ فَارْتَدَّ بَصِيْرًا  ؕۚ قَالَ اَلَمْ اَقُل لَّكُمْ ۚ ۙ اِنِّىْۤ اَعْلَمُ مِنَ اللّٰهِ مَا لَا تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(96)\nFALAMMAA AN JAAA-A AL-BASHEERU AALQAAHU A’LAA WAJHEHI FAARTADDA BASEERAA QAALAL ALAM AQUL LAKUM INNEE A-A’LAMO MENAL LAAHE MAA LAA TA’LAMOON.\nThen when the bearer of the good news came, He cast (the shirt) over his face, and he forthwith regained clear sight. He said: “Did I not say to you, 'I know from Allah that which ye know not?'“ \nقَالُوْا يٰۤاَبَانَا اسْتَغْفِرْ لَنَا ذُنُوْبَنَاۤ اِنَّا كُنَّا خٰطِئِيْنَ‏(97)\nQAALOO YAABAANAA ASTAGHFER LANAA ZUNOOBANAA INNAA KUNNAA KHAATE-EEN.\nThey said: “O our father! ask for us forgiveness for our sins, for we were truly at fault.” \nقَالَ سَوْفَ اَسْتَغْفِرُ لَكُمْ رَبِّىْؕ اِنَّهٗ هُوَ الْغَفُوْرُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(98)\nQAALA SAWFA AASTAGHFERU LAKUM RABBEAA INNAHU HOWA GHAFOORUL RAHEEM.\nHe said: “Soon will I ask my Lord for forgiveness for you: for he is indeed Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful.” \nفَلَمَّا دَخَلُوْا عَلٰى يُوْسُفَ اٰوٰٓى اِلَيْهِ اَبَوَيْهِ وَقَالَ ادْخُلُوْا مِصْرَ اِنْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ اٰمِنِيْنَؕ‏(99)\nFALAMMAA DAKHALOO A’LAA YOOSUFA AAAWAAA ELAYHE AABAWAYHE WA QAALA KHOLOO MESRA IN SHAAA-AL LAAHO AAAMENEENA.\nThen when they entered the presence of Joseph, he provided a home for his parents with himself, and said: “Enter ye Egypt (all) in safety if it please Allah.” \nوَرَفَعَ اَبَوَيْهِ عَلَى الْعَرْشِ وَخَرُّوْا لَهٗ سُجَّدًاۚ وَقَالَ يٰۤاَبَتِ هٰذَا تَاْوِيْلُ رُءْيَاىَ مِنْ قَبْلُقَدْ جَعَلَهَا رَبِّىْ حَقًّاؕ وَقَدْ اَحْسَنَ بِىْۤ اِذْ اَخْرَجَنِىْ مِنَ السِّجْنِ وَجَآءَ بِكُمْ مِّنَ الْبَدْوِ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ اَنْ نَّزَغَ الشَّيْطٰنُ بَيْنِىْ وَبَيْنَ اِخْوَتِىْؕ اِنَّ رَبِّىْ لَطِيْفٌ لِّمَا يَشَآءُؕ اِنَّهٗ هُوَ الْعَلِيْمُ الْحَكِيْمُ‏(100)\nRA-FA-A’ AABAWAYHE A’LAL A’RSHIL WAKHARROOA LAHU SUJJADANW WA QAALA YAA HAAZAA TAAWEELU RUYAAAAA MIN QABLUQAD JAA’ALAHAA RABBEE HAQQAN WA QAD AHSANAL BEE IZ AAKHRAJANEAA MENAL AS-SEJNE WA JAAA-A BEKUM MENAL AL-BADWE MIN BA’DE AN NNAZAGHA SHAYTAANO BAYNEE WA BAYNA AEKHWATEAA INNAL RABBEE LATEEFUN LEMAA YASHAAU INNAHU HOWA A’LEEM HAKEEM.\nAnd he raised his parents high on the throne (of dignity), and they fell down in prostration, (all) before him. He said: “O my father! this is the fulfilment of my vision of old! Allah hath made it come true! He was indeed good to me when He took me out of prison and brought you (all here) out of the desert, (even) after Satan had sown enmity between me and my brothers. Verily my Lord understandeth best the mysteries of all that He planneth to do, for verily He is full of knowledge and wisdom. \nرَبِّ قَدْ اٰتَيْتَنِىْ مِنَ الْمُلْكِ وَ عَلَّمْتَنِىْ مِنْ تَاْوِيْلِ الْاَحَادِيْثِ ۚ فَاطِرَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ اَنْتَ وَلِىّٖ فِى الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ ۚ تَوَفَّنِىْ مُسْلِمًا وَّاَلْحِقْنِىْ بِالصّٰلِحِيْنَ‏(101)\nRABBE QAD AAATAYTANEAA MENAL AL-MULKE WA A’ALLAMTANEAA MIN TAAWEELE AL-AAHAADEESE FAATERA SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE ANTA WALEAAA FIL DUNYAA WAL AAKHERAH TAWAFFANEAA MUSLEMAN WWAALHEQNEAA BE-SAALEHEEN.\n“O my Lord! Thou hast indeed bestowed on me some power, and taught me something of the interpretation of dreams and events, O Thou Creator of the heavens and the earth! Thou art my Protector in this world and in the Hereafter. Take Thou my soul (at death) as one submitting to Thy will (as a Muslim), and unite me with the righteous.” \nذٰلِكَ مِنْ اَنْۢبَآءِ الْغَيْبِ نُوْحِيْهِ اِلَيْكَۚ وَمَا كُنْتَ لَدَيْهِمْ اِذْ اَجْمَعُوْۤا اَمْرَهُمْ وَهُمْ يَمْكُرُوْنَ‏(102)\nZAALEKA MIN AANBAAE GHAYBE NOOHEEHE ELAYKA WA MAA KUNTA LADAYHIM IZ AAJMAU’OOA AAMRAHUM WA HUM YAMKOROON.\nSuch is one of the stories of what happened unseen, which We reveal by inspiration unto thee; nor wast thou (present) with them then when they concerted their plans together in the process of weaving their plots. \nوَمَاۤاَكْثَرُ النَّاسِ وَلَوْ حَرَصْتَ بِمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(103)\nWAMAAAAKSARU NAASE WA LAW HARASTA BE-MOAMENEEN.\nYet no faith will the greater part of mankind have, however ardently thou dost desire it. \nوَمَا تَسْئَلُهُمْ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ اَجْرٍؕ اِنْ هُوَ اِلَّا ذِكْرٌ لِّلْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(104)\nWA MAA TASALUHUM A’LAYHE MIN AAJRIN IN HOWA ILLAA ZIKRUNW LIL-A’ALAMEEN.\nAnd no reward dost thou ask of them for this: it is no less than a message for all creatures. \nوَكَاَيِّنْ مِّنْ اٰيَةٍ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ يَمُرُّوْنَ عَلَيْهَا وَهُمْ عَنْهَا مُعْرِضُوْنَ‏(105)\nWA KA-AYYIM MIN AAYATIM FIL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE YAMURROONA A’LAYHAA WA HUM A’NHAA MUA’REZOONA.\nAnd how many Signs in the heavens and the earth do they pass by? Yet they turn (their faces) away from them! \nوَمَا يُؤْمِنُ اَكْثَرُهُمْ بِاللّٰهِ اِلَّا وَهُمْ مُّشْرِكُوْنَ‏(106)\nWA MAA BIL LAAHE AKSAROHUM BIL-LAAHE ILLAA WA HUM MMUSHREKOONA.\nAnd most of them believe not in Allah without associating (other as partners) with Him! \nاَفَاَمِنُوْۤا اَنْ تَاْتِيَهُمْ غَاشِيَةٌ مِّنْ عَذَابِ اللّٰهِ اَوْ تَاْتِيَهُمُ السَّاعَةُ بَغْتَةً وَّ هُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُوْنَ‏(107)\nAAFAAMENOOA AN TAATEEHUM GHAASHEETUN MIN A’ZAABIN LAAHE AW TAA-TEYAHOMUL SAA-A’TO BAGHTATANW WA HUM LAA YASH-O’ROON.\nDo they then feel secure from the coming against them of the covering veil of the wrath of Allah, or of the coming against them of the (final) Hour all of a sudden while they perceive not? \nقُلْ هٰذِهٖ سَبِيْلِىْۤ اَدْعُوْۤا اِلَى اللّٰهِ ؔعَلٰى بَصِيْرَةٍ اَنَا وَمَنِ اتَّبَعَنِىْؕ وَسُبْحٰنَ اللّٰهِ وَمَاۤ اَنَا مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ‏(108)\nQUL HAAZEHI SABEELEAA AADU’OOA ELAL LAAHE A’ALAA BASEERATIN ANAA MANIT ATTABAA’ANEAA SUBHAANAL LAAHE WA MAA ANAA MENAL MUSHREKEEN.\nSay thou: “This is my way: I do invite unto Allah, on evidence clear as the seeing with one's eyes, I and whoever follows me. Glory to Allah! and never will I join gods with Allah!” \nوَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا مِنْ قَبْلِكَ اِلَّا رِجَالًا نُّوْحِىْۤ اِلَيْهِمْ مِّنْ اَهْلِ الْقُرٰىؕ اَفَلَمْ يَسِيْرُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ فَيَنْظُرُوْا كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْؕ وَلَدَارُ الْاٰخِرَةِ خَيْرٌ لِّلَّذِيْنَ اتَّقَوْا ؕ اَفَلَا تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(109)\nWA MAA ARSALNAA MIN QABLEKA ILLAA REJAALAN NNOOHEAA ELAYHIM MIN AHLIL AL-QURAA A-FALAM YASEEROO FIL ARZE FAYANZOROO KAYFA KAANA A’AQEBATUL LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM WALADAARU AAKHERATE KHAYRUL LIL-LAZEENA TAQAW AFALAA TA’QELOON.\nNor did We send before thee (as messengers) any but men, whom we did inspire, (men) living in human habitations. Do they not travel through the earth, and see what was the end of those before them? But the home of the hereafter is best, for those who do right. Will ye not then understand? \nحَتّٰۤى اِذَا اسْتَيْئَسَ الرُّسُلُ وَظَنُّوْۤا اَنَّهُمْ قَدْ كُذِبُوْا جَآءَهُمْ نَصْرُنَا ۙ فَنُجِّىَ مَنْ نَّشَآءُ ؕ وَلَا يُرَدُّ بَاْسُنَا عَنِ الْقَوْمِ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَ‏(110)\nHATTAA EZAA ASTAYASA ROSOLO WA ZANNOO ANNAHUM QAD KUZEBOOA JAAA-AHUM NASRUNAA FANUJJEAAA MAN NNASHAAU WA LAA YORADDO BAASUNAA A’NIL QAWMIL MUJREMEEN.\n(Respite will be granted) until, when the messengers give up hope (of their people) and (come to) think that they were treated as liars, there reaches them Our help, and those whom We will are delivered into safety. But never will be warded off our punishment from those who are in sin. \nلَقَدْ كَانَ فِىْ قَصَصِهِمْ عِبْرَةٌ لِّاُولِى الْاَلْبَابِؕ مَا كَانَ حَدِيْثًا يُّفْتَرٰى وَلٰكِنْ تَصْدِيْقَ الَّذِىْ بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ وَتَفْصِيْلَ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ وَّهُدًى وَّرَحْمَةً لِّقَوْمٍ يُّؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(111)\nLAQAD KAANA FEE QASASEHEM E’EBRATUN LEAOOLEAA AL-AALBAABE MAA KAANA HADEESAN YYUFTARAA WA LAAKIL TASDEEQA LAZEE BAYNA YADAYHE WATAFSEELA KULLE SHAY-IN WWAHUDAN WA RAHMATAL LEQAWMINY YOAMENOON.\nThere is, in their stories, instruction for men endued with understanding. It is not a tale invented, but a confirmation of what went before it, a detailed exposition of all things, and a guide and a mercy to any such as believe. ",
  "merits": "Surah Yusuf has 111 ayaat and was revealed in Makkah. It is narrated that the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said that whoever recites this Surah and teaches his family members how to recite it also, Allah (s.w.t.) will make the final moments before his death (sakaraatul mawt) easy for him to bear and will remove jealousy from his heart.\nIt has been narrated from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq that whoever recited this Surah daily, he will be raised on the day of Qiyamah with the handsomeness of Prophet Yusuf (a.s.) and he will be protected from the fear and discomfort of this day. He will be raised among the pious servants of Allah (s.w.t.). This Surah also keeps one’s heart safe from illegitimate lustful desires.\nThe sixth Imam (a.s.) has also said that if a person drinks the water in which this Surah has been dissolved, then his sustenance will be easier to reach and he will be made from the people of Jannah."
